    content: `
      <p class="eyebrow">BERT V2 / FundingPool</p><h1>Every USDC path<br /><span>has a named ledger.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">FundingPoolUpgradeable is V2 custody and accounting infrastructure, not a generic wallet. It separately tracks general deposits, author bonds, one wallet's pledge per funding round, round/idea escrow, pending fees, reserve and refund liabilities. Those ledgers determine what GrantManager may release, what reserve may retain and what voters can reclaim.</p>
      <h2>Public versus protocol-only calls</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Who calls it</th><th>Integration rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>deposit(amount)</code></td><td>Any wallet</td><td>General pool deposit; it is distinct from a pledge and creates no funding-round vote.</td></tr><tr><td><code>claimPledgeRefund(roundId)</code></td><td>Eligible pledge owner</td><td>Use only after direct settlement/refund preflight.</td></tr><tr><td><code>poolByRoundAndIdea</code>, <code>getPledge</code>, <code>previewRoundNetFunding</code></td><td>Read-only</td><td>Use for grant/refund presentation; do not derive entitlement from a raw USDC balance.</td></tr><tr><td><code>depositAuthorStakeFrom</code>, <code>recordPledgeFrom</code>, <code>openFundingRound</code></td><td>Registry / VotingSystem</td><td>Never call from an end-user UI; invoke the outer Registry or VotingSystem action.</td></tr><tr><td><code>finalizeFundingRoundFee</code>, <code>cancelUnclaimedFundingRound</code>, <code>activateGrantRefund</code>, <code>distributeFunds</code></td><td>Grant/distributor role</td><td>Observed through GrantManager; a wallet should not construct these calls.</td></tr><tr><td><code>receiveCommunityReserve</code></td><td>Authenticated V3 CommunityTreasury</td><td>Not an arbitrary cross-contract deposit path.</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <p>Index <code>FundingRoundOpened</code>, <code>PledgeRecorded</code>, <code>FundingRoundSettled</code>, <code>FundingRoundFeeFinalized</code>, <code>FundingRoundCancelled</code>, <code>GrantRefundActivated</code> and <code>PledgeRefundClaimed</code> alongside bond, distribution and reserve events. The event stream explains history; direct reads establish current spendability and refund eligibility.</p>
      <h2>Accounting surfaces</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Ledger / value</th><th>How it increases</th><th>How it decreases or changes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>totalPoolBalance</code></td><td>General deposits, bonds and pledges</td><td>Grant tranches and claimed refunds</td></tr><tr><td><code>authorStakeByIdea[id]</code></td><td>Author bond on idea creation</td><td>Explicit rejection slash zeros it and credits reserve</td></tr><tr><td><code>poolByRoundAndIdea[round][idea]</code></td><td>Pledges for that exact round and idea</td><td>Fee separation, grant tranches or eligible refund claims</td></tr><tr><td><code>pendingProtocolFeeByRound</code></td><td>Fee carved from a viable winner at settlement</td><td>Finalizes to reserve after claim, or restores on unclaimed-grant cancellation</td></tr><tr><td><code>protocolReserve</code></td><td>Rejected author-bond slashes, finalized success fees, authenticated V3 reserve inflows</td><td>Only configured reserve allocation paths</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <h2>USDC transfer paths</h2><ol class="numbered-flow"><li>A supporter may use <code>deposit(amount)</code>; it is a general pool deposit, not an idea pledge.</li><li>IdeaRegistry calls <code>depositAuthorStakeFrom</code> when a proposal is created.</li><li>VotingSystem calls <code>recordPledgeFrom</code> after all vote gates pass.</li><li>At viable settlement, FundingPool separates the winner's fee but does not reserve it yet.</li><li>At author claim, GrantManager finalizes the fee to <code>protocolReserve</code> and releases the first net-grant tranche.</li><li>Eligible pledge owners call <code>claimPledgeRefund</code>; no administrator distributes refunds for them.</li></ol>
      <h2>What a winning pool pays for</h2><p>At grant claim, GrantManager reads only the winner's <code>poolByRoundAndIdea[roundId][winningIdeaId]</code>, which is already net of the round fee. General deposits, losing pledges and an idea's author bond are never silently folded into grant escrow. The 30/40/30 schedule applies to that net amount.</p>
      <div class="callout warning"><strong>Frontends must read, not reconstruct.</strong> Indexer data is useful for history, but action availability and balances must be read from the contracts. A stale index can never make an unavailable grant, vote or reserve allocation valid.</div>
      <h2>Distribution finality</h2><p><code>distributeFunds</code> can only be called by the grant/distributor path, only while FundingPool is unpaused, and only up to the live per-round-per-idea amount. It marks <code>distributed[roundId]</code> true only once the remaining amount for that winning round becomes zero. GrantManager also records tranche flags before moving funds, preventing duplicate payment even when subsequent dependency calls revert.</p>
      <h2>Protocol reserve is not the dApp balance</h2><p><code>protocolReserve</code> is a dedicated accounting value inside FundingPool. It increases when an author bond is slashed, when a successfully claimed round finalizes its fee, or when an authenticated V3 Treasury routes defined reserve capital. It is not liquid user-owned pledge capital and is not a V3 Community Treasury balance.</p>
    `,
