    content: `
      <p class="eyebrow">BERT V2 / Integration safety</p><h1>Decode the revert.<br /><span>Preserve the invariant.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">A reverted transaction is often the protocol protecting an invariant, not merely an RPC failure. Decode custom errors with the same ABI used for simulation, map them to an actionable current-state read, and always accept the chain result as final.</p>
      <h2>Event subscription map</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Concern</th><th>Events</th><th>Client response</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Idea lifecycle</td><td><code>IdeaCreated</code>, <code>LegacyFundingProposalConfigured</code>, <code>IdeaStatusUpdated</code></td><td>Invalidate idea, target, profile and round queries.</td></tr><tr><td>Round lifecycle</td><td><code>VotingRoundStarted</code>, <code>VoteCast</code>, <code>VotingRoundEnded</code>, <code>FundingRoundOpened</code>, <code>FundingRoundSettled</code></td><td>Refresh active round, viability and result views.</td></tr><tr><td>Capital movement</td><td><code>PledgeRecorded</code>, <code>PledgeRefundClaimed</code>, fee/reserve and distribution events</td><td>Refresh pledge preview, refund claims and FundingPool reads.</td></tr><tr><td>Grant lifecycle</td><td><code>RoundFunded</code>, <code>UnclaimedGrantExpired</code>, <code>GrantCancelled</code>, milestone events</td><td>Refresh payout, deadline and request state for that round.</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <h2>Core invariants</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Invariant</th><th>How V2.2 enforces it</th><th>Integration implication</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Idea lifecycle is forward-only</td><td>IdeaRegistry allows a fixed transition graph and terminal statuses.</td><td>Never offer a manual reopen or status repair action.</td></tr><tr><td>One wallet, one pledge per round</td><td><code>hasVoted</code> and FundingPool's pledge record both lock the voter before/with transfer.</td><td>Changing the selected idea after submission is not a V2 feature.</td></tr><tr><td>Pledges remain idea-specific</td><td>FundingPool stores one <code>ideaId</code> and amount per voter/round.</td><td>Never describe a losing pledge as grant capital for another idea.</td></tr><tr><td>Only a viable idea wins</td><td>VotingSystem compares net funding after the snapshotted fee with each target.</td><td>Render the target and net-funding preview, but use settlement as final.</td></tr><tr><td>Round fee is contingent</td><td>Fee finalizes only after <code>claimGrant</code>; cancellation restores it.</td><td>Do not report reserve revenue merely when voting ends.</td></tr><tr><td>Milestones and refunds cannot pay twice</td><td>Payout flags, request state and per-pledge claim flags gate each terminal payment.</td><td>Wait for confirmed state after each transaction.</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <h2>High-signal failure conditions</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Failure</th><th>Typical cause</th><th>Correct next check</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>HumanVerificationRequired</code></td><td>PoP gate is enabled and the wallet lacks an active record.</td><td>Read verifier state; on Arc Testnet use only labelled Demo verification.</td></tr><tr><td><code>InvalidMinimumFunding</code></td><td>Target is zero or a configured legacy target is being set twice.</td><td>Read <code>minimumNetFundingByIdea</code> and choose a non-zero target.</td></tr><tr><td><code>NotEnoughIdeas</code></td><td>Fewer than 30 unused configured pending ideas are available.</td><td>Read <code>canStartNewRound()</code> and live counters.</td></tr><tr><td><code>AlreadyVoted</code></td><td>Wallet already committed its one pledge in that round.</td><td>Read <code>hasVoted</code>; do not retry with another idea.</td></tr><tr><td><code>PledgeRefundUnavailable</code></td><td>Round is not settled, caller has no pledge, or winner grant remains live.</td><td>Read settlement, caller pledge and grant cancellation state.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GrantClaimExpired</code></td><td>Author attempted to claim at or after the 14-day deadline.</td><td>Offer public <code>expireUnclaimedGrant</code>, not a late author claim.</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <h2>Pause is an explicit safety state</h2><p>VotingSystem, FundingPool and GrantManager have independent pause controls. A paused contract blocks its protected write paths even if the other modules are healthy. Treat pause as a state to display plainly, not a condition to work around with retries or alternate function calls.</p>
      <div class="callout warning"><strong>Proxy safety is separate from user safety.</strong> V2 modules are upgradeable contracts. Their proxy/role administration must be controlled operationally, while normal user interfaces should rely on the current implementation's public read and write interface only.</div>
      <h2>Incident-quality report</h2><p>For any unexpected V2 behavior, record the network, contract address, transaction hash, caller, function arguments, observed event logs, expected invariant and actual result. Avoid publishing a potentially exploitable proof before using the private disclosure channel in the Testnet guide.</p>
    `,
